---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="BABAI — Run your business without leaving WhatsApp"
  description="BABAI is a business operating platform built around WhatsApp, designed to turn customer conversations into business workflows."
>
  <header class="wrap topbar">
    <a class="brand-lockup" href="#top" aria-label="BABAI home">
      <span class="brand-symbol" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/products/babai/brand/babai-monochrome-face.jpeg" alt="" width="1254" height="1254" /></span>
      <span><span class="brand-name">BABAI</span><span class="product-tag">A NEKURAMA PRODUCT</span></span>
    </a>
    <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
      <a href="#workflow">How it fits together</a>
      <a href="#focus">Initial focus</a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main id="main" class="wrap">
    <section class="hero" id="top" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Business operations, around WhatsApp</p>
        <h1 id="hero-title">Run your business without leaving WhatsApp.</h1>
        <p class="lede">BABAI is a business operating platform built around WhatsApp. It is designed to turn customer conversations into the work that follows: orders, restaurant operations, and fulfillment.</p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href="#workflow">See how it fits together <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
          <a class="button secondary" href="#channels">WhatsApp + web</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="workflow-visual" role="img" aria-label="Illustration of a customer conversation becoming a structured pickup order and restaurant task">
        <div class="visual-top"><span><span class="live-dot"></span>Conversation to operation</span><span>01 / 03</span></div>
        <div class="flow-line" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="chat-card first" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="chat-head"><span class="avatar">C</span><span>Customer conversation</span></div>
          <p>“Can I order two masala dosas for pickup?”</p>
          <span class="message-chip">Menu context · pickup</span>
        </div>
        <div class="chat-card second" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="chat-head"><span class="avatar">B</span><span>Structured order</span></div>
          <p>2 × Masala dosa<br />Pickup · awaiting confirmation</p>
          <span class="message-chip">Ready for the restaurant</span>
        </div>
        <div class="flow-stamp" aria-hidden="true"><strong>Human in control</strong>Review and take over when needed</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="workflow" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">The operating flow</p>
        <div>
          <h2 id="workflow-title">One conversation. A coordinated next step.</h2>
          <p>When a request becomes an order, its details need to carry through menu selection, restaurant review, fulfillment, and customer updates. BABAI is designed to connect these steps while keeping staff in control. This describes product direction, not a claim that every integration is available today.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li class="step"><h3>Conversation</h3><p>Understand the customer's question or request in the business context.</p></li>
        <li class="step"><h3>Menu</h3><p>Use the restaurant's catalog and availability as the reference.</p></li>
        <li class="step"><h3>Pickup order</h3><p>Shape the request into an order the business can review.</p></li>
        <li class="step"><h3>Restaurant operations</h3><p>Accept, prepare, and update the order with staff in control.</p></li>
        <li class="step"><h3>Completion</h3><p>Record payment status and share supported order updates.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="channels" aria-labelledby="channels-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Two connected surfaces</p>
        <div>
          <h2 id="channels-title">Act in WhatsApp. Configure and review on web.</h2>
          <p>“Without leaving WhatsApp” describes the primary conversational experience. BABAI is not WhatsApp-only: web supports work that benefits from a larger, denser view.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="channel-grid">
        <article class="channel whatsapp"><p class="eyebrow">Primary conversation surface</p><h3>WhatsApp</h3><p>Customer questions, menu and order interactions, status messages, staff actions, and human takeover are designed around the business's own WhatsApp identity.</p></article>
        <article class="channel"><p class="eyebrow">Supporting productivity surface</p><h3>Web</h3><p>Use a larger view for configuration, menu review, order operations, comparison, analytics, recovery, and multi-branch administration as the product evolves.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="focus" aria-labelledby="focus-title">
      <div class="focus">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">First validation scope</p><h2 id="focus-title">Start narrow.<br />Learn from the work.</h2></div>
        <div class="focus-copy">
          <p class="scope-label">Restaurant-first · pickup-first</p>
          <p>The initial validation scope is one restaurant, one branch, and one business WhatsApp number. It keeps pickup first, includes human fallback, and has no delivery dependency.</p>
          <p>This describes the pilot scope, not general availability, customer traction, or proof of product-market fit.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="footer">
    <div class="wrap footer-inner"><span>BABAI — a product of Nekurama</span><a href="/">About Nekurama <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
  </footer>
</SiteLayout>
